# Cursor Rules for Personality Architect Mini App

## Neynar Integration
- Using @neynar/nodejs-sdk v3.34.0
- API client configured in src/lib/neynar.ts
- Functions: getUserProfile(fid), publishCast(signerUuid, text, embeds)
- API Key stored in NEYNAR_API_KEY environment variable

## Neynar API Documentation
- OpenAPI Spec: https://github.com/neynarxyz/OAS/
- Node.js SDK: https://github.com/neynarxyz/nodejs-sdk
- Official Docs: https://docs.neynar.com
- MCP Setup Guide: https://docs.neynar.com/docs/neynar-farcaster-with-cursor

## Key Neynar Methods & Patterns

### Client Initialization
```typescript
import { NeynarAPIClient, Configuration } from "@neynar/nodejs-sdk";
const client = new NeynarAPIClient(new Configuration({ apiKey: process.env.NEYNAR_API_KEY }));
```

### Fetching Users
- `fetchBulkUsers({ fids: number[], viewerFid?: number })` - get user profiles
- Returns `BulkUsersResponse` with `users: User[]` array
- User object has: `fid`, `username`, `display_name`, `pfp_url`, `profile?.bio?.text`, `follower_count`, `following_count`

### Publishing Casts
- `publishCast({ signerUuid: string, text?: string, embeds?: PostCastReqBodyEmbeds[], ... })` - publish casts
- Returns `PostCastResponse` with `cast.hash` property
- Requires signer UUID (not just signer string)

### React Components
- @neynar/react package available: NeynarProfileCard, NeynarCastCard, NeynarAuthButton, etc.
- See docs/NEYNAR_UI_COMPONENTS_ANALYSIS.md for details

## Project Structure
- Next.js 15.4.6 with React 19
- TypeScript 5
- Supabase for database/auth
- Farcaster Miniapp SDK for client-side
- Neynar SDK for server-side Farcaster operations

